# PYRAMID — Project Brief for Claude Code
> Read this at the start of every session before writing any code.

---

## What is this game?

Pyramid is a **turn-based roguelite dungeon climber** played in the browser. The player builds a party of up to 6 characters and climbs a pyramid-shaped dungeon, room by room, toward the top. The dungeon is made of triangular rooms — you can only move to rooms that share a side with your current room. The game has three acts, each its own pyramid. Die, and you lose your run — but permanent upgrades and discovered characters carry forward into the next run, compounding over dozens of runs.

The core fantasy: **the same warrior you start with on run 1 becomes something terrifying by run 30.** Long-term investment should feel meaningful and visible.

Inspirations: Slay the Spire (map navigation, act structure), Soda Dungeon (party building, class stacking), Dead Cells (meta-progression, permanent upgrades).

---

## What does it feel like to play?

- Strategic but accessible. Decisions matter but should feel readable.
- Each run feels different because of random room contents and path choices.
- Characters feel distinct — a Warrior and a Wizard should play completely differently.
- Progression feels rewarding — upgrades between runs should be noticeable.
- Ancient civilisation × fantasy aesthetic. Think Egyptian pyramids meets DnD.

