## Core Design Rules — NEVER break these

1. **Data-driven.** Never hardcode an enemy, item, or class inside logic files. All definitions live in data files (enemyData.js, itemData.js, etc.). Logic files read from data files.

2. **One responsibility per file.** damageCalc.js only calculates damage. renderer.js only draws. If a file is doing two things, it should be two files.

3. **No global variables except state.js.** All shared state lives in state.js and is imported explicitly.

4. **Every function does one thing.** Small, named, readable functions. No 100-line functions.

5. **Comment your code.** Every function gets a one-line comment explaining what it does.

6. **When unsure about a design decision — STOP and ask the developer before proceeding.** Do not make assumptions about game design. Do make assumptions about code structure if it's unambiguous.

