## The Stats System

Every character and enemy has exactly these 7 stats:

| Stat | What it does |
|------|-------------|
| HP   | Total hit points |
| DEF  | Flat damage reduction per hit |
| DMG  | Base damage multiplier |
| DEX  | Crit chance, dodge, trap avoidance |
| SPD  | Initiative order in combat |
| INT  | Scales spell damage, determines mana pool size |
| LUCK | Affects crit, loot quality, event outcomes |

Stats have three layers:
- **Base** — the class's starting value
- **Permanent** — added by meta-upgrades (persists across all runs, affects all instances of that class)
- **Run** — gained via leveling and equipment (lost on death)

**Final stat = base + permanent + run bonuses**

---

## The Classes

| Class | Role | Signature Mechanic |
|-------|------|--------------------|
| Warrior | Tank / CC | Taunt (force enemies to target him) |
| Barbarian | Berserker | Rage state: +DMG, -DEF |
| Cleric | Healer / Spellcaster | Divine Pact, unlockable subclasses |
| Archer | Fast sniper | High SPD, status applier |
| Wizard | AoE nuke | Highest INT, glass cannon |
| Paladin | Hybrid tank-healer | Holy Shield, anti-undead bonus |
| Summoner | Indirect damage | Summon familiars into combat |

Classes are **discovered** during runs (first encounter = permanently unlocked). Multiple instances of the same class can exist in one party. Permanent upgrades affect ALL instances of a class.

---

## Combat System

- **Turn-based, initiative order** based on SPD stat (highest goes first)
- On your turn: Basic Attack / Special Ability (costs mana) / Use Item / Defend
- **Mana pool** = INT × 5. Regenerates INT/10 per turn. Does NOT reset between fights.
- **Damage formula:** Attacker DMG × ability multiplier − Defender DEF (minimum 1)
- Crits triggered by DEX/LUCK check, multiply damage 1.5–2.5×
- Status effects: Poison, Burn, Stun, Bleed, Taunt, Rage, Shield, Slow, Bless, Curse

