## The Pyramid

- Each act = one pyramid, **15 layers deep**
- Layer N has (2N − 1) triangular rooms. Total = 225 rooms per pyramid.
- Player visits ~15–30 rooms per act due to path constraints.
- **Adjacency rule:** you can only enter a room that shares a side with your current room.
  - Upward triangle (△): connects to left neighbor, right neighbor, and the downward triangle above it.
  - Downward triangle (▽): connects to left neighbor, right neighbor, and the upward triangle below it.
- **Lazy generation:** only generate a layer when the player first reaches the layer below it. Never generate the full pyramid upfront.
- 3 acts per run. Boss always at the top triangle of each act.

### Room Types
| Type | Notes |
|------|-------|
| Combat | Standard fight. Most common. |
| Elite Combat | Harder enemy, better rewards. |
| Shop | Spend gold. |
| Event | Narrative choice, risk/reward. |
| Treasure | Free loot. |
| Rest | Heal party HP. |
| Trap | Surprise damage/debuff. DEX helps avoid. |
| Ambush | Combat where enemies act first. |
| Warp | Teleport to random room next layer. |
| Boss | Fixed at pyramid apex. Cannot skip. |

---

## Meta Progression

- **Soul Shards** — single meta-currency. Earned by completing rooms, defeating bosses, discovering classes.
- Spent between runs on permanent stat upgrades per class.
- Upgrade trees have 3–5 nodes per stat. Later nodes unlock new mechanics, not just bigger numbers.
- **Evolved forms** unlock at upgrade thresholds (e.g. Warrior → Warlord). New name, altered kit.
- **Item unlocks:** items found for the first time enter the loot pool for all future runs.

---

## Equipment

Each character has 3 slots: **Weapon, Armor, Accessory**
- Weapons + Armor = stat bonuses
- Accessories = passive relic-style effects (e.g. "first hit each combat is always a crit")
- Rarities: Common / Uncommon / Rare / Legendary

